    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong></p><p>Boyle’s Law [1 mark]</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong></p><p>- <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P_1V_1 = P_2V_2\"></span><br/><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100 \\cdot 4.0 = P_2 \\cdot 2.0 \\Rightarrow P_2 = \\frac{400}{2.0} = 200\\ \\text{kPa}\"></span><br/>- Correct equation and substitution [1 mark]<br/>- Correct final answer with unit [1 mark]</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong></p><p>As volume decreases, particles collide more frequently with the walls, increasing the pressure. [1 mark]</p></section>"
